bad_logic: git log --merges --max-count=1 is NOT HEAD-scoped
  - It searches the git log history (reflog + commit history) for the most recent merge commit anywhere
  - If the repo has ANY merge commit in history, git log --merges --max-count=1 returns that commit
  - Even if current HEAD is single-parent (non-merge), the command still returns the last merge from history
  - This caused single-parent commit 8d95e58 to be incorrectly flagged as a merge commit

why false positive happened:
  - is_merge_commit() called git log --merges --max-count=1
  - Repository history contained merge commit f072bd8a
  - Command returned "commit f072bd8a" regardless of current HEAD state
  - is_merge_commit() returned True even though HEAD (8d95e58) was single-parent
  - This caused PRE_R049 round-id gate to incorrectly skip validation for single-parent HEAD
  - The 8d95e58 rollback detected this and rolled back to e1b929b (single-parent state)

corrected logic:
  - git rev-list --parents -n 1 HEAD returns EXACTLY the current HEAD commit and its parents
  - Output format: "<commit_hash> <parent1> <parent2> ..." (space-separated)
  - tokens = result.strip().split()
  - parent_count = len(tokens) - 1
  - parent_count >= 2 → merge commit (True)
  - parent_count <= 1 → non-merge commit (False)
  - No history search, no reflog, no message inspection

why corrected logic is safe:
  - Completely scoped to HEAD: only queries the current commit's parent list
  - Single-parent HEAD returns ["hash"] → parent_count=0 → False
  - Two-parent HEAD returns ["hash", "p1", "p2"] → parent_count=2 → True
  - Octopus merge returns ["hash", "p1", "p2", "p3", ...] → parent_count≥3 → True
  - git failure → except block → return False (fail-closed)
  - No reliance on commit message text
  - No reliance on history traversal
  - Works with shallow clones (fetch-depth=1) because it only reads the local commit object

relation to 8d95e58 rollback:
  - 8d95e58 was a single-parent commit on canonical
  - is_merge_commit() returned True due to history containing f072bd8a merge
  - Rollback detected this and restored HEAD to e1b929b (single-parent state)
  - Rollback detected the bug but could not fix it (only rollback)
  - Forward repair v2 now properly fixes the root cause: HEAD-scoped structural detection
  - Rollback conclusion remains unchanged (e1b929b state was correct)
  - Forward repair v2 confirms the rollback was correct and fixes the underlying detection bug

confirmation:
  - Rollback itself did NOT fix is_merge_commit()
  - Rollback was necessary and correct (single-parent HEAD should not be flagged)
  - Forward repair v2 provides the permanent fix by replacing the broken detection method
  - The fix is minimal (single function, single file) and targeted